From 47e1697decef25223b31db4e01ead172b65f3bf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:36:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(interaction): predict held trapdoor placement

Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5 retains the first locally predicted trapdoor
facing, half and world hit during held placement, including camera and
material changes. Repeated placement adds closed neighbors instead of
toggling the previous block. Release restores ordinary interaction.

Send physical use lifetimes through the shared channel and retire them
on release, screens, disconnect and connection replacement. Suppress block
activation after successful trapdoor placement and preserve independent
water, power and material properties. Separate trapdoors and the original
support remain eligible; unrelated non-trapdoor targets do not.

Prediction format 2 carries placement/interaction/failure and the native
cursor immediately before the concluding Java sequence. Native snapping
expresses the original world hit relative to each later target, even
outside its unit cube. Keep that cursor separate from the Java raycast
packet and clear it with the held placement state. Failed height-limit
attempts do not capture a placement until prediction succeeds.

Use the existing Java 3/16 trapdoor outline for fresh clicks instead of
the approximate 0.1825 custom outline. Native and Java bottom-face hits
then agree at 0.8125.

Native, direct Java and ViaProxy Survival fixtures accept the same server
facing correction when the new camera direction precedes placement.
Earlier teleport fixtures placed before the native camera update and
did not establish a server direction lock. Preserve authoritative states
instead of forcing the locally predicted facing back onto the world.

Real block-state tests cover orientation, materials, independent
properties, target eligibility, frozen world hits, release and ordinary
blocks. Matching native evidence also covers item consumption, pause
cancellation and replacement after server removal. Captures stay private.
